<title>RUSSIA: Russia '97 non-CIS natural gas exports seen rising.</title>
<headline>Russia '97 non-CIS natural gas exports seen rising.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian exports of natural gas outside the Commonwealth of Independent States are expected to rise to 138 billion cubic metres (bcm) in 1997 from 128 bcm in 1996, Fuel and Energy Minister Pyotr Rodionov said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>He earlier forecast 1997 output to rise to 614 bcm from 601 bcm in 1996.</p>
<p>Rodionov submitted his resignation last week. No successor has been named.</p>
<p>-- Mike Collett-White, Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
